        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Southwell, Nottinghamshire, England; Truro, Cornwall\n- Organizations: Southwell Minster; Truro Cathedral; Church of England\n- People: Rev. John Thomas Becher\n- Roles: English clergyman; social reformer; Vicar-General\n\nFacts:\n- Rev. John Thomas Becher was born in 1770 and died in 1848.\n- Rev. John Thomas Becher was an English clergyman and social reformer.\n- From 1818 to 1840, Rev. John Thomas Becher served as Vicar-General of Southwell Minster.\n- Southwell Minster is a minster and cathedral in Southwell, Nottinghamshire, England.\n- Truro Cathedral, formally the Cathedral of the Blessed Virgin Mary, Truro, is a Church of England cathedral in Truro, Cornwall.",
